#: src/security.md:1
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:3
msgid "This page covers the security design."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:5
msgid "Unsafe Rust"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:7
msgid ""
"Some parts of the system code use unsafe Rust code which has less compiler "
"verification than safe Rust, thus still safer than C or C++"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:9
msgid ""
"Unsafe Rust code is replaced with safe Rust code where possible, where it's "
"not possible the security focus relies on boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:11
msgid ""
"Some unsafe Rust code is using safe Rust code in some parts, we are looking "
"more unsafe Rust code than can use safe Rust code."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:13
msgid "Applications and Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:15
msgid ""
"The POSIX and Linux source code compatibility don't reduce the system "
"security, `relibc` translate POSIX APIs and try to improve the compatibility "
"security where possible:"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:17
msgid ""
"The microkernel architecture greatly reduce the potential to use system bugs "
"to get application or library sensitive data or inject malicious code"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:18
msgid "POSIX and Linux functions are written in Rust, which prevent many bugs"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:19
msgid "Input sanitization is done where possible, like strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:21
msgid ""
"The POSIX/Linux applications or libraries is who decide if they use safer "
"APIs, while Redox provide the compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:23
msgid "Capabilities and Sandbox"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:25
msgid ""
"The namespaces and [capability-based](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Capability-based_security) system are implemented by the kernel but some "
"parts can be moved to user-space."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:26
msgid ""
"A namespace is a list of schemes, if you run `ls :`, it will show the "
"schemes on the current namespace."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:27
msgid "Each process has a namespace."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:28
msgid ""
"[Capabilities](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"File_descriptor#File_descriptors_as_capabilities) are customized file "
"descriptors that carry specific actions."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:30
msgid ""
"The sandbox system duplicates the system resources for each program, it "
"allows them to be completely isolated from the main system. Flatpak and Snap "
"use a sandbox security system on Linux, Redox will do the same."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:32
msgid "Redox allows sandbox by limiting a program's capabilities:"
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:34
msgid ""
"Only a certain number of schemes in the program's namespace is allowed, or "
"no scheme at all. That way new file descriptors can't be opened."
msgstr ""

#: src/security.md:35
msgid "All functionality is forced to occur via file descriptors (WIP)."
msgstr ""
